  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% failure rate as a corrective-action trigger rather than a sales bar, with no sales-stop consequence, while giving customers complete per-model results and keeping public publication off. S3 sets new-unit shut-off at 24 months and retrofit at 6 years, and S5 keeps the 8-per-100k recall trigger but lets the regulator substitute corrective action without a time limit, which is the open-ended exception the Ember 8 (9.9) would need. S1 is strong (24-hour serious-incident reporting, 7-day other reporting and customer notice), and S4 sets built-in suppression at 36 months."
 },
